{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook","id":70424,"title":"Shouldn't Timeline Splinters be in general corebook?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-12T01:31:24-08:00","id":70424,"title":"Shouldn't Timeline Splinters be in general corebook?","content":"I'm just starting to read Demon, but was interested in Timeline Splinters, so I quick searched the corebook, and couldn't find them. Asked for help on forums, and was a bit surprised that all the info on them are in Seatlle City section. I know that city setting need something cool to have in ti, but Splinters rules and description should be in main corebook, I think. Otherwise people will look for it in wrong places, just like me. There Seatlle section can have accurate description of what they look like in the city. That's mine opinion, but I think it's logical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T04:29:42-08:00","id":70479,"title":"","content":"Timeline splinters aren't necessarily a common experience, though. While I imagine a lot of people are thinking of ways to incorporate them into cities where their games are taking place, they don't seem to be universal enough to be considered a mainstream phenomenon. Especially since certain facets of the ones described in the book are particular to Seattle (particularly the sheer number of them and the way the 1889 splinter behaves).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:26:06-08:00","id":70735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=70479#post70479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since certain facets of the ones described in the book are particular to Seattle (particularly the sheer number of them and the way the 1889 splinter behaves).</div> </div> </div> </div>That the Hallows of Awakened are the most numerous in Boston, or bigest Hedge is in Maiami, don't mean those things aren't in other places. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T11:33:33-08:00","id":70738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=70735#post70735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That the Hallows of Awakened are the most numerous in Boston, or bigest Hedge is in Maiami, don't mean those things aren't in other places. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge is not a localized phenomenon geographically confined to a particular city and Hallows aren't solely created as the direct or indirect result of the machinations of a transcendent techno-deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:23:32-08:00","id":70777,"title":"","content":"I use four splinters in Los Angeles in our game ; our favorite is the 'Gestapo 71' timeline, where our resident Inquisitor agency resides in a timeline roughly based on the book 'Fatherland' where Hitler won the war. Though the Agency doesn't have direct nazi allegiances they DO dress up in black trenchcoats with skulls all the time, so it makes trading with them interesting!<br /> <br /> I also have a 1984 timeline, and a timeline where the Zombie Plague has essentially rendered Los Angeles into a L4D timezone.<br /> <br /> The Eastern Columbia building, the largest clock tower in Los Angeles, is the Lynchpin which holds the four Timelines in place. That structure holds multiple secret methods of conveyance to each, carefully hidden via infrastructure. You'll note it has four giant clockfaces. Each is 'anchored' in a separate timeline.<br /> <br /> I've implied that Angels somewhat eschew the other Timelines, which has led my players to speculate that those are not 'primary' timelines and that the God Machine is running them on 'minimal power'. That may or may not be true ; I'm considering whether to drop them into a future timeline, too, just to make them question whether they're really the prime one or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T14:16:28-08:00","id":70834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=70738#post70738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge is not a localized phenomenon geographically confined to a particular city and Hallows aren't solely created as the direct or indirect result of the machinations of a transcendent techno-deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't any clear description that Splinters are result of machintion of God Machine. Only that he is using them. For all we know, Splinters can be made by True Fae or Archmages. Or even just &quot;natural phenomenon&quot; in World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> And I only point to this - if Splinters ARE somehow repetetive phenomeneom, world-wide, even if not that popular as Hallows, they should be descibed in proper corebook, not in city's setting section. That's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T14:27:28-08:00","id":70853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=70834#post70834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't any clear description that Splinters are result of machintion of God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent Corebook, page 248 (first page of Appendix: Seattle, second column, first complete paragraph)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Just prior to the Great Seattle Fire of 1889, God-Machine agents completed an occult matrix that would allow the timeline \u2014 at that point, the only timeline for the region \u2014 to branch, creating a limited 1889 Seattle that never moves forward \u2014 almost like saving a video game.</b> The fire destroyed the city proper but led to a renaissance, causing the city to double in size and technological capability within two years. The need for the prior bubble time was erased and the process forgotten \u2014 but not deleted. Whether it was intended to be undone or is simply held in reserve is a matter for debate among Inquisitors, but it still exists despite the century that has passed in the main timeline. Whatever its original reason for existing, what is clear is that more splinters have cropped up over the passing of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very extremely clear description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-12-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T15:30:11-08:00","id":70888,"title":"","content":"Seems like Time Travel is a God Machine domain, I suspect. It'd be an awesome place to have, oh, a Delorian. Maybe a Time Flux Capacitor or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T11:36:15-08:00","id":72105,"title":"","content":"In one of the splinters you go to, all the vampires like to talk about the Camarilla and the Sabbat, the werewolves are all worried about the Wyrm, Mages are fighting with techno-dudes, an the local demons all call themselves Slayers and Defilers and stuff. Oh, and the Changelings are totally bonkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T12:40:02-08:00","id":72150,"title":"","content":"You're trying to say changelings aren't totally bonkers Here?<br /> If so you haven't been paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T14:56:37-08:00","id":72247,"title":"","content":"Page 73 of the God-Machine book has the first example of a splinter time-line under &quot;Sister City&quot;. Demon just expanded on the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T17:11:11-08:00","id":72331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=72247#post72247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 73 of the God-Machine book has the first example of a splinter time-line under &quot;Sister City&quot;. Demon just expanded on the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>But rules and advice on interactions of demons with Splinters are not in proper corebook, only in setting appendix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T18:00:18-08:00","id":72351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=72331#post72331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But rules and advice on interactions of demons with Splinters are not in proper corebook, only in setting appendix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Sister City is a story focused around the potential collision of the 1889 splinter with the dominant timeline - and it's also set in Seattle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T18:29:50-08:00","id":72371,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry Wyrd. I just don't understand what you're saying. The Appendix is a proper place in the core. It's &quot;Hey, here's some extra stuff. Oh yeah remember how we mentioned this in a different book. Here's the expansion!&quot; Everything in Demon, is proper for Demon. Since Demon's interact with the G-M. It was added. But since the original introduction of Splinters was in the GMC that doesn't make it exclusive to Demon and there's no reason to put that rule set next to the rest of the crunch, like with the exploits, embeds ect. <br /> I'm sorry you had confusion finding it, but it only makes sense to keep those thoughts together. The Seattle section has information on splinters, so that's where the rules belong. If anything, dealing with Splinters should have been given more information in GMC; they were that cool. But we were lucky enough to get them in Demon, which I don't think anyone expected. <br /> Demon's don't have sole rights to the splinters, nor are Splinters a result of Demonic presence if they were. If they were, the search for Hell wouldn't be nearly as mysterious. Like Embeds, they're just aware of their existence and use them. Other splats probably aren't aware of them as a whole but doesn't mean they don't get involved every so often. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:06:23-08:00","id":72717,"title":"","content":"I wonder what the relationship between Splinters and the shatterverse style shard realms introduced in Mirrors. While, sure Mirrors was pre GMC, but I imagine that alternate/parallel splinters can be vastly different and not necessarily focused on time. I like the extreme examples above, of a Fatherland-like state and an OWoD like state. In my PCs group, theres some less-than-serious fourth wall breaking jokes about God and the Exarchs ending the OWoD and causing a new reality. I decided to turn that into a dark, serious plotline when an error in the local reality matrix caused duplicates of PCs and NPCs to appear, but made with OWoD fluff (a lot of the PCs were actually converted/redone for NWoD from CWoD). I'd like to go all out, and equate the interactions with Splinters to the interactions with the Shatterverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T23:19:32-08:00","id":73041,"title":"","content":"I could imagine the Shatter being a splinter that broke when Reality did; the Shatter kept a lot more of the mystical stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:39:28-08:00","id":75221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=70834#post70834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I only point to this - if Splinters ARE somehow repetetive phenomeneom, world-wide, even if not that popular as Hallows, they should be descibed in proper corebook, not in city's setting section. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're very rare. I don't want to say they're absolutely unique, in case we have a great idea for them in the future, but there are currently no plans for them beyond Seattle, which they were specifically created for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T11:48:11-08:00","id":78475,"title":"","content":"There's also going to be a whole book on Seattle, and the splinters will get more attention there. <br /> <br /> I should start redlining that, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T22:21:16-08:00","id":81950,"title":"","content":"I had a weird feeling when I started to read about the splinters.<br /> I really loved everything I read until then.<br /> But suddenly, I was wondering why do we need these splinters and all this time-travel thing in a game about Demons, that is already so rich with its own theme?<br /> I was confused, and I am still: those splinters seem very important, but I'm not really willing to put them at the center of a campaign, while there is so much that can be done about the morality, the humanity, the feelings, ... of the characters/players.<br /> I haven't read yet the scenario at the end of the book but saw it was related to the splinters, so maybe I'll have a better sense of what can be done with them when I'm done with it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my 2 cents on that topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1841-nflagey","name":"nflagey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T22:46:06-08:00","id":81959,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that splinters are a rare phenomenon manufactured by the God-Machine. And for that reason alone do they have some coverage in Demon. Your city might not have a Splinter, your Demon's may not ever experience one. But in the back of their heads that are likely aware of the possibility that such things do exist. It's no different than the reason why the various Agenda's have a blurb about the other splats. It's not that Demon needs interaction with the rest of the WoD splats but if they do, here's a handy guide. Splinters were first introduced in the GMC book. They just go more cover here, and will get more again. I find them interesting, but I would be hard pressed to use one myself. And if I do, it would be later in my game than something that's just looming over the players heads the whole time. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T00:02:40-08:00","id":81973,"title":"","content":"Well, that's not what it looks like after reading the section on Seattle. Basically, after reading a couple 100s of pages of exciting pages on Demons (I really enjoyed my reading!), I was struck by, what I felt was a sudden change of theme: time travel. It is omnipresent in the section, and while it is here and there linked to the God Machine, the whole Demonic theme got king of lost in my head at that point. I would surely play a bit with 1 splinter, as one of the many aspects of the God Machine, but having 4 of them in the main city of the book seems overwhelming to me.<br /> Please be sure that I love your work, and that, as for Demon The Fallen, I rarely enjoyed reading a role playing corebook that much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1841-nflagey","name":"nflagey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:32:13-08:00","id":82229,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really strike me as Time Travel though. You're not going back into the past to alter anything, and what you view is merely an alternate probability. The Splinters are Time-Line splinters. Not time travel pockets (There's a couch in a diner that does that if I'm not mistaken) and no matter what you do in them the clock is going to reset to square one. Unless you manage to get the splinter to bleed over and fuse with the rest of the world. Have you seen fringe? They're more like alternate worlds, only you can run amok and have little consequences for doing so. That being said, I'd rather that the Time-Line splinters didn't reset, I find that bit lack luster and were I to open a way splinter in a game it wouldn't reset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T16:05:57-08:00","id":82382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/70424-shouldn-t-timeline-splinters-be-in-general-corebook?p=82229#post82229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really strike me as Time Travel though. You're not going back into the past to alter anything, and what you view is merely an alternate probability. The Splinters are Time-Line splinters. Not time travel pockets (There's a couch in a diner that does that if I'm not mistaken) and no matter what you do in them the clock is going to reset to square one. Unless you manage to get the splinter to bleed over and fuse with the rest of the world. Have you seen fringe? They're more like alternate worlds, only you can run amok and have little consequences for doing so. That being said, I'd rather that the Time-Line splinters didn't reset, I find that bit lack luster and were I to open a way splinter in a game it wouldn't reset.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a situation in the anime <i>Kamisama no Inai Nichiyoubi</i> (loosely translated as <i>The Sunday Without God</i>) that's very much like a splinter - entering a particular door leads to a version of the abandoned town that's thoroughly populated.<br /> <br /> The characters are led there by the newest member of their group and thus receive a bit of advance warning about the place: on the same day every year, the entire world resets (the character in question has actually tried burning down the town a few times to no avail), rewriting the memories of anyone inside (including newcomers - the town incorporates them on the next loop, as the character discovered when he tried bringing in more people and the town simply grew to accommodate them), and the entire reason the place exists seems to be owed to the apparent fact that God started granting wishes before He went away and the students of a particular class wanted to undo the on-campus death of a classmate.<br /> <br /> It's very difficult to leave the place and the character who knows about all of this (who is one of two people who aren't subject to the memory-rewrite) has been trying to force the bubble to burst for a couple of years by the time the characters reach the town.<br /> <br /> It's the subject of an entire arc of the show and it and the Seattle splinters have seemed resonant with similar concepts, though the 1889 splinter's having broken the temporal loop sometime in the last few decades seems like it would cover much of the groundwork for making splinters that aren't time-locked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T18:14:08-08:00","id":82428,"title":"","content":"I'm really into alternate dimension stuff like that, and I could always use a new anime. Thanks for the heads up, I'll take a peek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T18:34:19-08:00","id":82442,"title":"","content":"The cities in the Seed Collection all have at least one Splinter, if I remember right. Looking forward to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T19:54:02-08:00","id":82465,"title":"","content":"Is there word on which cities were getting in the seed collection? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}